prompt:
Kreative Studio pose editor, image check part (STU-PE3). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no build step. The same file runs in Node 22 (CommonJS require) and in the browser (classic <script>, no modules). Use exactly this wrapper and nothing outside it:

(function () {
  'use strict';
  const NS = typeof module === 'object' && module.exports ? null : (globalThis.KKPose = globalThis.KKPose || {});
  const need = (name, file) => (NS ? NS[name] : require(file));
  // ... the code; get other pose modules with need('vec', './vec.js') INSIDE functions, never at the top level (load order in the browser is free) ...
  const api = { /* exported names */ };
  if (NS) NS.<NAME> = api; else module.exports = api;
})();

Do not change the test file. Return the whole file.

Write public/js/pose/posefit.js (NAME = posefit): fit the target pose to what a generated image shows, and give the fix as PE1 set_joint ops. Angles are degrees.

Other pose modules (get them with need() inside functions): FK = need('fk', './fk.js'): solve(pose) -> world w. P = need('project', './project.js'): makeView(opts, w) -> view with view.width, view.height, view.scale, view.center (when opts has scale AND center, the camera is fixed to them; otherwise it fits w); keypoints(view, w) -> kp. PC = need('posecheck', './posecheck.js'): BONES (list of {name, a, b, joint}, parents first), compare(target, detected, opts) -> {pass, swapped, worst, tol, bones: [{name, joint, err, status}]}, swapSides(kp). S = need('skeleton', './skeleton.js'): S.byName[joint].limits = {bend: [min, max], side: [min, max], twist: [min, max]}. OPS = need('ops', './ops.js'): clamp(joint, e) -> {bend, side, twist} inside the limits.

A pose is {version: 1, root: {pos}, joints: {name: {bend, side, twist}}}; a missing joint or key means 0.

TWIST_PARENT = {l_forearm: 'l_shoulder', r_forearm: 'r_shoulder', l_shin: 'l_hip', r_shin: 'r_hip'}.

Export:
- fit(pose, detected, opts = {}): tol = opts.tol ?? 20; view = opts.view || {}.
  1. w0 = FK.solve(pose); v0 = P.makeView(view, w0); cam = {...view, width: v0.width, height: v0.height, scale: v0.scale, center: v0.center}. kpOf(p) = (w = FK.solve(p), P.keypoints(P.makeView(cam, w), w)).
  2. before = PC.compare(kpOf(pose), detected, {tol, swap: opts.swap}); det = before.swapped ? PC.swapSides(detected) : detected.
  3. p = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(pose)); p.joints = p.joints || {}.
  4. For each b of PC.BONES in order: errOf(q) = the err of bone b.name in PC.compare(kpOf(q), det, {tol, swap: false}) (Infinity when it is null). If that bone's status in the current p is not 'wrong', go on to the next bone.
     vars = [[b.joint, 'bend'], [b.joint, 'side']], plus [TWIST_PARENT[b.name], 'twist'] when TWIST_PARENT has b.name. get(q, [j, k]) = (q.joints[j] && q.joints[j][k]) || 0. with(q, [j, k], x) = a copy of q whose joints[j] = OPS.clamp(j, {...q.joints[j], [k]: x}).
     Coarse grid: every combination of values, each var from its limit min to max in steps of 15 (the max itself included); start from best = p, bestErr = errOf(p), and take a grid pose only when its err is smaller than bestErr.
     Refine: for step of [8, 4, 2, 1, 0.5, 0.2, 0.1]: repeat while something improved: for each var, for d of [step, -step]: q = with(best, var, get(best, var) + d); if errOf(q) < bestErr - 1e-9, best = q and bestErr = errOf(q).
     Then p = best, with every value of the vars' joints rounded to 0.1 and passed through OPS.clamp again.
  5. ops: for each joint name in p.joints whose OPS.clamp(name, p.joints[name]) differs from OPS.clamp(name, pose.joints && pose.joints[name]) in bend, side or twist: {op: 'set_joint', joint: name, bend, side, twist} with p's clamped values (keys in this order).
  6. after = PC.compare(kpOf(p), detected, {tol, swap: opts.swap}). Return {pose: p, ops, before, after, swapped: before.swapped}. Never change the input pose.
- regions(target, detected, check, opts = {}): boxes for repainting the wrong bones. pad = opts.pad ?? 24; det = check.swapped ? PC.swapSides(detected) : detected. For each bone in check.bones with status 'wrong', bd = the PC.BONES entry with the same name; pts = the a and b points (average of the listed indices) of target and of det, skipping null ones. box = [Math.floor(minX - pad), Math.floor(minY - pad), Math.ceil(maxX + pad), Math.ceil(maxY + pad)], then x clamped to 0..detected.width and y to 0..detected.height. Return [{bone, joint, box}] in check.bones order.
